From 9a4ef9996079bd4865effd1c01fad96e8062faaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruben Herold <ruben@puettmann.net>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:06:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: batch a hard clear of peers when an address family is
 given

A clear that names an address family is not batched, because bgp_clear()
only opens a clearing batch when neither AFI nor SAFI is given. Every
peer is then cleared on its own, with a full table walk per peer, and
bgpd is blocked while it runs. "clear ip bgp" counts as well, it sets
the family to IPv4.

A hard clear resets the whole session whatever family is given, the
family only selects the peers. Batch it like a clear without a family.
Soft clears stay as they are.

A peer that is added to a batch returned from bgp_clear_route_all()
before rfapiProcessPeerDown(), so VNC kept the routes of that peer.
This was already the case for the clears that were batched before,
and it now would reach one more clear command. Call it for batched
peers as well, it only starts the withdraw timers of the routes of
the peer and does not depend on the table walk.

Add a topotest that clears a peer-group with a family, checks that only
the member with that family is reset, and that a clearing batch ran.

Signed-off-by: Ruben Herold <ruben@puettmann.net>
(cherry picked from commit 6cbd8cc66a10a1bf9a9363fc567d74d71540b6f6)
---
